     "], "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True]}, FrameRate -> 10,
    AnimationRunning -> True, AnimationRepetitions -> DirectedInfinity[1], 
   "MaxSize" -> {680, 340}], 
  "Figure 5. Top-down view of the same scene.  Same metric, same bubble \
velocity, same spacecraft, but no z-axis cosmetics so the geometry is \
unobstructed.  The red crescents are the actual analytic Eulerian \[Rho] \
(more red = more exotic matter required); the cyan grid is the ", 
  StyleBox["instantaneous", FontSlant -> Italic], " coordinate distortion ", 
  "\!\(\*StyleBox[\"x\", \"TI\"]\) \[RightArrow] \!\(\*StyleBox[\"x\", \
\"TI\"]\) + 0.5\!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\"\[Beta]\", \
\"x\"]\)(\!\(\*StyleBox[\"t\", \"TI\"]\))", 
  " \[LongDash] a snapshot of the metric geometry at each frame, scaled by \
0.5 for visibility \[LongDash] not a Lagrangian-advected mesh, so it returns \
to a flat grid wherever the bubble is far away.  Compare with Figure 6 below, \
which shows the genuinely cumulative displacement of comoving test particles. \
 The dashed white circle is the nominal bubble radius."]], "Input",ExpressionU\
UID->"edae3765-a2fa-4009-b0e2-1c89a062d31d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both animations are rendered entirely from the analytic Alcubierre formulas \
\[LongDash] no GR solver, no NDSolve, just the closed forms for the shape \
function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"f", "(", 
    SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "59028727-d99e-4376-b329-98436b258b32"],
 ", the shift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "x"], "=", "-", 
    SubscriptBox["v", "s"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "196519a3-0766-4e77-a91a-f658f270e9c2"],
 ", and the Eulerian energy density.  Both run in seconds.  The spacecraft \
mesh and animation logic add fewer than 200 lines of Wolfram on top of the \
existing package."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc848240-7ecb-4319-bf04-ba01dd578487"],

Cell["6. The grid being warped", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1833c30d-6796-407f-91b4-461e6558d3fc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Another way to see what the bubble is doing to the geometry is to drop a \
regular Cartesian grid into the spacetime and let the shift field advect \
every grid intersection.  As the bubble sweeps from left to right across the \
frame the grid lines locally bunch up in front of it and stretch out behind \
it.  The animation below uses a 15\[Times]15 grid, the analytic Alcubierre \
shift field with v=c and R=1, and a simple Euler advection step following the \
Eulerian-observer law ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"d", 
    SuperscriptBox["x", "i"], "/", "dt"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "73e3f71c-dce3-4414-b336-37da12385856"],
 "=",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "2a105840-dd20-4f8e-b690-657892f4857f"],
 "=",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["v", "s"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "6c6d05f6-d545-4c13-9c72-5991a0dd20ce"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01c166d1-c7c5-415a-b2f9-2e6bf5ec8f66"],

Cell["\<\
alcShift[t_, x_, y_] := +1.0 TanhShape[Sqrt[(x - 1.0 t)^2 + y^2], 1, 8];
(* alcShift returns +v_s f = -beta^x = Eulerian 3-velocity. *)

advect[{x0_, y0_}, t_, nstep_] := Module[{x = x0, y = y0, dt = t/nstep},
  Do[{x, y} = {x + dt alcShift[k dt, x, y], y}, {k, 0, nstep - 1}];
  {x, y}];

frame[t_] := Show[
  DensityPlot[
    AlcubierreExpansionScalar[{1, 1, 8}, {t, x, y, 0}],
    {x, -3, 3}, {y, -2.5, 2.5},
    ColorFunction -> \"RedBlueTones\", Frame -> True,
    PlotLegends -> Automatic],
  Graphics[{Thickness[0.0015], Black,
    Table[Line[Table[advect[{x, yi}, t, 14], {x, -3, 3, 6/60}]],
          {yi, -3, 3, 6/14}],
    Table[Line[Table[advect[{xi, y}, t, 14], {y, -3, 3, 6/60}]],
          {xi, -3, 3, 6/14}]}]];
ListAnimate[Table[frame[t], {t, 0, 2, 2/29.}]]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"09345dac-c825-418a-a623-5a0089a9d450"],

