     "], "Byte", ColorSpace -> "RGB", Interleaving -> True]}, FrameRate -> 6, 
   AnimationRunning -> True, AnimationRepetitions -> DirectedInfinity[1], 
   "MaxSize" -> {540, 457}], "Figure 6. A regular Cartesian grid ", 
  StyleBox["cumulatively", FontSlant -> Italic], 
  " advected by the Alcubierre shift field as the bubble sweeps from left to \
right.  Each grid intersection is a comoving test particle: once the bubble \
has pushed it, it stays at its new position because the shift field provides \
no restoring force \[LongDash] this is why the grid stays deformed behind the \
bubble, in contrast to the ", 
  StyleBox["instantaneous", FontSlant -> Italic], 
  " coordinate-distortion mesh in Figure 5.  The background colour is the \
Eulerian expansion scalar \[Theta] (red = contraction in front of the bubble, \
blue = expansion behind).  Inside the bubble all four points of any small \
grid cell move together \[LongDash] no internal stretching, no tidal forces.  \
All the deformation is concentrated in the wall."]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"8cb86bf0-16e3-4cb3-94d3-a951384e3891"],

Cell["7. Geodesics: getting swept up by a warp bubble", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d3d5b46b-5c59-44ae-972b-2193dd6cb691"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Drop a population of test particles into the spacetime and let them follow \
geodesics.  Free-fall trajectories ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], "(", "\[Lambda]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "568173cc-91b1-47cf-a38b-f0b63b4e4392"],
 " obey the geodesic equation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"705ceea1-fd12-42ef-9d6e-7e5baeb023d1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["d", "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"]}], 
    RowBox[{"d", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "2"]}]], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Alpha]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], " ", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Beta]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"]}], "=", "0"}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"a1386908-d44e-4cc7-ac93-94f74863722f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which we rewrite as a first-order ODE system for position and 4-velocity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"d", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], "/", "d\[Lambda]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "62b93b80-26a0-42c5-b8e8-f7a0a5264d20"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fddf9d21-7286-4aba-9807-ae73bd276776"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"]}], ",", 
   "\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]\[ThickSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"d", 
      SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"]}], "d\[Lambda]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Alpha]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Beta]"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",\

 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"432704fa-de03-4e08-9e90-d0ad1ed387b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For massive (timelike) particles the affine parameter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Lambda]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "22d87096-abe8-4d1e-924e-03b6b422601a"],
 " can be chosen to be the proper time, and the velocity is normalised so that"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f0edbf7a-019e-45ca-817f-e977c08ee18c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["g", 
    RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Mu]"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["u", "\[Nu]"], "=", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->"7c933415-df67-4fa0-94bf-eb9f3c401548"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For light rays (null geodesics) the normalisation becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["g", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]"}]], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["k", "\[Mu]"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["k", "\[Nu]"], "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "3db9cc0a-d17e-459a-ba50-afe6249d8cb8"],
 " instead, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Lambda]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "87d91517-fa26-4a2e-9cac-73c79cf0ed67"],
 " is no longer proper time (which is zero for a photon) but any affine \
parameter along the ray.  The Christoffel coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", 
    RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "8385a938-302e-4d74-9dfe-2931cd027f3a"],
 " in the right-hand side are the same expressions Wolfram generated \
symbolically in Section 3 \[LongDash] we just substitute the current ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["x", "\[Mu]"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "d1fad5dc-b968-4bb0-be4e-f18f5020e1b1"],
 " values into them and hand the result to ",
 StyleBox["NDSolve", "Input"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"de5b7085-89c4-4a08-b98d-1f59601a1800"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In ADM language an Eulerian observer (the analogue of a stationary one in \
flat space) has spatial 3-velocity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"-", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "b70459a5-0076-4d4c-8777-bece160fee0f"],
 " = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["v", "s"], " ", 
    RowBox[{"f", "(", 
     SubscriptBox["r", "s"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Times",ExpressionUUID->
  "ab7dd8de-a06f-474b-bf22-0beeffc32062"],
 " (positive, forward).  We place eight initially stationary particles ahead \
of the bubble; as the bubble overtakes them from behind, each one is grabbed \
by the shift field and dragged forward.  Particles on the bubble axis get the \
deepest grip; particles further off-axis are partly missed by the wall and \
feel proportionally less drag:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"116b2cd9-2c32-4b33-8e42-a0be07e3b9af"],

Cell["\<\
alcShift[t_, x_, y_] := +1.0 TanhShape[Sqrt[(x - 1.0 t)^2 + y^2], 1, 8];

(* Eulerian-observer advection: dx/dt = -beta^x = +v_s f(r_s).
   alcShift here returns the magnitude +v_s f, which is exactly
   -beta^x for an Alcubierre bubble.  Use a fixed Euler step. *)
sweep[{x0_, y0_}, ts_] := With[{dt = ts[[2]] - ts[[1]]},
  FoldList[
    {#1[[1]] + dt alcShift[#2, #1[[1]], y0], #1[[2]]} &,
    {x0, y0}, Rest[ts]]];

ts = Range[0., 4., 0.05];
trajs = Table[sweep[{2., y0}, ts], {y0, Range[-1.4, 1.4, 0.35]}];
ListAnimate @ Table[
  Show[DensityPlot[
         AlcubierreExpansionScalar[{1, 1, 8}, {ts[[k]], x, y, 0}],
         {x, -1, 6}, {y, -2, 2}, PlotPoints -> 90,
         ColorFunction -> \"RedBlueTones\", PlotLegends -> Automatic],
       Graphics[{Black, Thick, Line /@ (Take[#, k] & /@ trajs),
         Red, PointSize[0.022], Point /@ (#[[k]] & /@ trajs)}]],
  {k, 1, Length[ts], 2}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellTags->"runnable",ExpressionUUID->"847f7ca6-6d58-4609-b5fc-ca67c6fe7826"],

